{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you tonight. Can you tell me what brought you to the hospital?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:14:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’ve had this terrible headache for about a week. It’s on the left side, throbbing, and I get really sensitive to light. I’ve also been nauseous and threw up a few times."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:15:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And has this happened before? Does it feel like your usual migraines?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:16:05",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it’s similar, but this one feels worse. I also noticed my blood pressure was really high at home—202 over 121. My usual is around 170 systolic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:17:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s quite high. We checked your BP here and it was 197 over 122. We gave you a dose of labetalol to help bring it down. We also did a CT scan of your head—it came back normal, which is good news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:18:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. But why is the headache so bad? I’ve had pseudotumor cerebri before—could that be it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:19:55",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s possible. Because of your history, the neurology team recommended a lumbar puncture to check your spinal fluid pressure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:21:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, right—I remember that. It hurt a little, and I had sudden pain in my lower left belly during it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:22:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we saw that. You had an episode of left lower quadrant pain during the LP, so we did a CT of your abdomen and pelvis to be safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:23:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And what did it show?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:24:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No signs of appendicitis, kidney stones, or other bowel issues. There’s a small calcified structure in your pelvis, but it’s unchanged from past imaging and likely not causing problems."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:25:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good. What about the spinal tap?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:26:35",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The opening pressure was high, which supports pseudotumor cerebri. We removed 23 cc of fluid, which often helps relieve headache pressure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:27:50",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Did it help?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:28:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You mentioned your headache improved a bit after that, which is a good sign. We also started you on IV fluids, Zofran for nausea, and morphine for pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:29:25",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I felt a little better overnight. But I still feel nauseous."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:30:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re aware. We’re going to continue IV fluids and add Reglan, another anti-nausea medication that often works well when Zofran isn’t enough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:31:55",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thank you. What about my liver tests? I saw the nurse mention something."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:33:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good question. Your liver enzymes—ALT and AST—were elevated. We think this is because you’ve been taking Percocet and Tylenol every 6 hours at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:34:25",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was trying to keep up with the headache pain. Is that dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:35:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Both contain acetaminophen. Taking them together like that can overload your liver. We’ve stopped all acetaminophen-containing meds here. Your liver values are already improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:36:55",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t realize they were both the same. I’ll be more careful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:38:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. When you go home, you can take Percocet as needed, but if you use Tylenol, limit it to 500mg every 6 hours—or just use one or the other. Never exceed 4 grams of acetaminophen per day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:39:25",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. What about my blood pressure? It’s usually high, but I’ve felt dizzy since I got here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:40:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your BP dropped quite a bit—some readings were around 100 over 60. Since your baseline is higher, we held several of your BP meds to avoid going too low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:41:55",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Which ones did you stop?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:43:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re holding spironolactone, amlodipine, and HCTZ for now. You’ll continue lisinopril and clonidine. We’ll adjust labetalol too—down to 100mg twice a day instead of 200mg three times."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:44:25",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if my pressure goes up again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:45:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If your systolic goes above 160, you can restart your previous doses of labetalol and spironolactone. But please follow up with your PCP soon to review this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2137-10-13 01:46:55",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I have an appointment next week. Will I need new meds for the headaches?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2137-10-14 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Yes, we’re restarting two preventive medications: topiramate and acetazolamide (Diamox). They help reduce fluid buildup and prevent migraines and pseudotumor flares."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2137-10-14 09:16:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I took those before. Diamox made my fingers tingle."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2137-10-14 09:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a common side effect and usually not dangerous. Let your neurologist know if it bothers you. We’re starting at low doses to help you adjust."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2137-10-14 09:18:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. My headache is much better now, mostly just a dull ache. And the belly pain is gone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2137-10-14 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great progress. We’re switching you from IV morphine to oral oxycodone for any breakthrough pain. And you’re keeping fluids down, so we’ll transition Reglan to oral as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2137-10-14 09:21:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be able to go home tomorrow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2137-10-14 09:22:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you keep improving, yes. We’ll monitor you today, and if your nausea stays under control and you’re stable, we’ll plan for discharge tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2137-10-15 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you’re doing well. Your labs are stable, headache is resolved, and you haven’t vomited in over 24 hours. We’re going to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2137-10-15 10:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2137-10-15 10:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue the new headache meds—topiramate twice daily and Diamox twice daily. Take Reglan for nausea if needed. Follow the acetaminophen limits, and monitor your blood pressure closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2137-10-15 10:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my BP meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2137-10-15 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take lisinopril, clonidine, and the lower dose of labetalol. Hold the others unless your systolic goes above 160. Discuss everything with your PCP at your appointment this week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2137-10-15 10:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What signs should I watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2137-10-15 10:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Return to the ER if you have worsening headache, vision changes, dizziness, chest pain, or high fever. Otherwise, follow up with your neurologist about the new medications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2137-10-15 10:08:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel much better and more confident going home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2137-10-15 10:09:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. It was good taking care of you. Take care and get some rest."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2137-10-13 01:13:00",
